# villa-haiku: required elements

Coordinates are the plan's (x 0..35, y 0..9, z 0..47; street at z<0; front faces north). Floor layer y1, air y2..5, roof y6..9.
Vocabulary names are defined in plan.md (VOCABULARY). `*` = added by the designer, not named in the brief.

| # | Element | Real construction (block by block) | Coordinates | Part | Vocab |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| E01 | Symmetrical street front | North wall z=0 x0..35, cream plaster `smooth_quartz` y2..5, facade raised to y9 under the street roof; red `red_terracotta` dado y2..3; pilasters are the shop partition ends at x15 and x20 | z=0, x0..35 | shell | plaster, dado |
| E02 | Recessed entrance (fauces) | Pocket: z=0 x16..19 y2..5 carved to air (1 deep). Door set back at z=1: `dark_oak_door` x17 and x18, y2..3 (two leaves, hinges outside). Jambs `quartz_block` at x16 and x19 (z=1, y2..3). Lintel `smooth_quartz` at z=1 x17..18 y4..5. Pediment: 4-wide `quartz_stairs` triangle at z=0 (y6 x16..19, y7 x17..18) | pocket z=0; door z=1; pediment y6..7 | shell (pocket, door), roofs (pediment) | doorway, door, pediment |
| E03 | Shuttered shop rooms (4) | Four shops W1 x1..7, W2 x9..14, E2 x21..26, E1 x28..34 (z1..7). Each street opening 4 wide, 3 tall (y2..4) carved to air. Shutters flank each opening: `dark_oak_trapdoor[open=true]` on the wall cell at y2..4 (x1 and x6 for W1; x9 and x14 for W2; x21 and x26 for E2; x29 and x34 for E1). Counter: `smooth_quartz` at z=1, y2 across the opening | openings x2..5, x10..13, x22..25, x30..33 at z=0 | shell (openings, shutters), facade (counter) | shopOpening, shutter |
| E04 | Atrium, open to the sky | Floor mosaic y1 x10..25 z9..20; air y2..5; walls `smooth_quartz` at x9 and x26 (z9..20) and z21; the roof is a ring of four shed bands with a void in the middle (see E06) | x10..25, z9..20 | shell (walls), roofs (ring) | mosaicFloor |
| E05 | Impluvium (rain pool) | Rim: 6x6 ring at y1 x15..20 z12..17, `smooth_quartz_slab` bottom. Water: `water` source in the 4x4 centre x16..19 z13..16 at y1 (floor y0 is solid, so it holds) | x15..20, z12..17 | atrium | impluvium |
| E06 | Compluvium (square opening in the roof) | 6x6 void in the roof directly over the impluvium: no roof blocks at x15..20, z12..17, y6..9. The four roof bands stop at its edges | x15..20, z12..17 | roofs | (void) |
| E07 | Tablinum facing the entrance | Study room at the far end of the atrium on the axis. Opening from the atrium: x14..21, y2..4 at z=21 (lintel y5). Back doorway to the peristyle: x16..19, y2..4 at z=26. Walls `smooth_quartz` at x12 and x23 | air x13..22, z22..25 | shell, interior designer | (room) |
| E08 | Peristyle garden court | Walkway ring x9..26 z27..40 (floor mosaic). Court x12..23 z30..37 with `grass_block` at y1. Beds and hedges inside (E10, E11). Path legs `smooth_stone` at y1 x17..18 z27..29 and z38..40 | court x12..23, z30..37 | peristyle | bed, hedge |
| E09 | Covered colonnade of white columns | Columns `quartz_pillar` (axis y) y2..4 with `quartz_slab` capital at y5 (bottom half). N row z29 x11,14,21,24; S row z38 x11,14,21,24; W column x11 z32,35; E column x24 z32,35. Ring roofs (E18) cover the walks | see list | peristyle | column |
| E10 | Formal planting (four beds) | Grass beds: W x13..14 z31..36, E x21..22 z31..36, plus N and S beds z30 and z37 (the hedges' inner rows). Planted: `rose_bush` at the bed corners (2-high), `cornflower` and `poppy` (1-high) on the rest | beds in court | peristyle | bed |
| E11 | Low hedges | 1-high `azalea_leaves` at y2 on the court perimeter: z30 and z37 rows (x12..16 and x19..23, gap at the axis x17..18), x12 and x23 columns (z31..36). Hedge sits on the grass | perimeter of court | peristyle | hedge |
| E12 | Fountain | Basin: 6x6 rim (E05 style) x15..20 z31..36 at y1, `smooth_quartz_slab`, with water x16..19 z32..35 at y1. Centre column `quartz_block` x17..18 z33..34 y2..3. Jet: `water` at (17,4,33) on the column top | basin x15..20 z31..36 | peristyle | fountain |
| E13 | Statues (two) | Plinth `polished_andesite` at y2, figure `oxidized_copper` y3..5 (3 blocks). Set in the beds at x13 and x22, z33 (mirror pair) | (13,2..5,33), (22,2..5,33) | peristyle | statue |
| E14 | Triclinium: dining room, couches on three sides | Room x12..23 z42..46. Couches on three sides: W side x13 and E side x22 (z43..45), S side z45 (x14..21). Each couch is a row of `dark_oak_stairs` at y2 facing the table, with `red_carpet` at y2 in front. Table centre `dark_oak_slab` on `quartz_pillar` stub. Doorway from the peristyle x16..19 at z=41 | air x12..23, z42..46 | interior (triclinium designer) | couch, table |
| E15 | Cubicula (small bedrooms) | Five bedrooms: W-N x1..8 z9..13; W-S x1..8 z15..20; W-P x1..7 z29..38; E-P x28..34 z29..38; E-S x27..34 z15..20. Floor mosaic, plaster walls, one bed each (`red_wool` head and `dark_oak_stairs` frame, as the designer chooses) | see rooms | interior designers | bed |
| E16 | Kitchen (culina) with hearth | Room x27..34 z9..13. Hearth: `stone_bricks` pad x31..32 z10..11 with `campfire[lit=true]` at (31,2,10); `smoker` nearby. Window x35 z11..12 | air x27..34, z9..13 | interior (culina designer) | hearth |
| E17 | Mosaic floors | Floor layer y1 in every room and the walkways: `white_terracotta` field, `black_terracotta` border, `red_terracotta` central medallion in the atrium and tablinum | all interior y1 | shell | mosaicFloor |
| E18 | Terracotta tile roofs sloping inward to the courts | Shed bands (see plan ROOFS). Palette: `bricks` 3 : `red_nether_bricks` 2 (the tile field), eave `bricks`, ridge `quartz_slab`, verge `quartz_block`. Stairs derived by the roof tool | y6..9 over all ranges | roofs | roofBand |
| E19 | Cream plaster walls with red dado | Walls `smooth_quartz` y2..5. Dado: `red_terracotta` at y2..3 on every interior and outer wall face | all wall cells | shell | plaster, dado |
| E20 | Bronze lamps | Standing lamp: `quartz_pillar` at y2 on the floor, `lantern[hanging=false]` at y3 on it. Placed at the pocket (16,2,0) and (19,2,0), the street (13,1,-2) and (22,1,-2), the atrium corners (10,2,9), (25,2,9), (10,2,20), (25,2,20) | see plan | facade, atrium | lamp |
| E21 | Potted plants | `flower_pot` with `potted_fern` or `potted_azalea_bush` standing at y2 on the floor. Atrium corners, tablinum sides, peristyle walkway ends | see plan | atrium, interior designers | pot |
| E22 | Shuttered shop rooms, shutters (see E03) | `dark_oak_trapdoor[open=true]` on the wall face at y2..4 flanking each shop opening | see E03 | shell | shutter |
| E23 | Main entrance door | `dark_oak_door` x17..18, y2..3, z=1 (E02) | see E02 | shell | door |
| E24 | Storerooms (cellae) | Four rooms: W x1..11 z22..25, E x24..34 z22..25, SW x1..10 z42..46, SE x25..34 z42..46. Plain floors, `barrel` and `smooth_quartz` stacks by the designers | see rooms | interior designers | (room) |
| E25 | *Windows on outer walls | `iron_bars` grilles 1x2 at y3..4 on the outer walls of cubicula, kitchen and triclinium (see plan OPENINGS) | outer walls | shell | window |
| E26 | *Street paving | `stone_bricks` at y0 in front of the facade, z=-4..-1, x12..23 (the approach), with `smooth_stone` edge slabs at z=-1 | z -4..-1 | facade | (ground) |
| E27 | *Roof eaves over the walkways | Colonnade lean-to roofs on the peristyle ring, eaves at y6, outer walls to y8 | ring | roofs | roofBand |

Built by the shell part (ticked): E01, E02 (pocket, door pair, jambs, lintel; the pediment is the roofs part's), E03, E04, E17 (floors; the atrium medallion is left, the impluvium takes the centre), E19, E22, E23, E25.
